From d20513c2fd9de4e7b48190f32da5f01f7b8d7f04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:51:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] settings_ui: the Agent Sandbox page speaks pt-BR (zeo_i18n's
 first screen)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 2 of docs/I18N-PROPOSAL.md (zeo-workspace): the Agent Sandbox (ai-jail)
page -- its notices, the two lists, the limits, the host switches, the
capabilities, the generated command, the other projects' defaults and the
Memory section -- reads its text through zeo_i18n's t! (0177) from
locales/<language>/agent-sandbox.ftl, in en-US and pt-BR.

The en-US file is the page's own English, byte for byte, so the page reads
as it did and every existing test still pins the same text (the catalog is
English until zeo_i18n::init, which tests never call). What used to be built
by concatenation is now a whole message per case: "Writable folder ... is
already in the list" and its siblings select on $kind (rw_map, allow_host),
the limit labels on $field, the memory scope on $source, so a language writes
the article and the agreement English does not need. pt-BR also gets plurals
English never had ("1 página").

The pt-BR text was drafted with Lara Translate and revised by hand: jail,
sandbox and thread stay English (the operator's glossary, 2026-11-24), and
"MCP Servers" too, since it names Zed's own page. Not translated yet: the
page's title in the settings navigation ("Agent Sandbox (ai-jail)", matched
by title elsewhere), errors and dialogs that come from the agent_sandbox crate
(validation, Turn Off, Forget), and the thread's jail status and quick modal
in agent_ui.

SettingsInputField::with_placeholder takes impl Into<SharedString> instead of
&'static str: a translated placeholder is owned. Every existing caller passes
a literal, which still converts. The placeholder is set when the field's
editor is created, so a language change reaches it when the page reopens.

In the ai-jail group, after 0175: every file it edits belongs to that group.
